fluxecho.module.sky_sails=Sky Sail Array
tile.fluxecho.module_core.sky_sails.name=Sky Sail Array Core
fluxecho.sky_sails.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's sky sails§r\nA bridge cabin on a floating platform and six masts, three huge sails of light spread between them, turned toward the sun\nEach mast keeps a sail; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.sky_sails.structure=§bThe Sky Sail Array: a floating platform 21×21 and 15 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on the sky ring (S2 first, then S6) once the Sky Sail Array is researched (phase IV) and the dome generator's pod floats: the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start. The job also lays the catwalk from the pod and opens the pod's door to it\n· A platform of Floating Foundation level with the pod's floor, railed round but for the catwalk's mouth; a bridge cabin at the front (walls 4 high, the kit portal, a back door, two holo pedestals inside) and six masts behind it in three pairs (a plinth, a Sample Socket, ten posts and a crown, 13 high), the light sails drawn between each pair\n· 6 units, 6 samples: each mast's plinth and socket; right-click either holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the array\n· The core in the cabin's portal between its two doors, two blocks above the deck, facing the pod\n· Made of Floating Foundation and frame parts, Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, posts, plinths, crowns, rails, holo pedestals and Sample Sockets (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
